        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Washington, D.C.; District of Columbia\n- Organizations: Howard University Hospital; Freedmen's Hospital; Providence Hospital; The New Freedmen's Clinic; Howard University College of Medicine\n- Places/Structures: Griffith Stadium\n- People: Haskell \"Hal\" Small\n- Roles: composer; pianist; music teacher\n\nFacts:\n- Haskell \"Hal\" Small was born on 3 June 1948.\n- Howard University Hospital, previously known as Freedmen's Hospital, is a major hospital in Washington, D.C., built on the site of the former Griffith Stadium.\n- Providence Hospital is a 408-bed hospital located in the District of Columbia.\n- The New Freedmen's Clinic first opened in the summer of 2009.\n- The New Freedmen's Clinic is a free student-run health care clinic affiliated with Howard University Hospital and Howard University College of Medicine.\n- Haskell \"Hal\" Small is a composer, pianist, and music teacher in Washington, D.C.",
